cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GIGNN, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: GIGNN
abstract: "Python implementation of the geographically informed graph neural network (GIGNN) proposed in the paper below. Following the spatial statistic trinity framework, GIGNN leverages attribute differences by spatial stratified heterogeneity, quantifies connections between geographical entities, and applies k-order neighbour attribute aggregation and message passing for spatial simulation and prediction."
